WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.864
Every evening the card network sends 30 refunds.

2
00:00:05.864 --> 00:00:11.204
In a lakehouse table, those rows sit inside Parquet files that are never changed.

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.443
A file's columns are compressed, and its footer records their sizes and min and max values.

4
00:00:17.443 --> 00:00:20.232
Change one value and all of that is wrong.

5
00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:23.153
So every correction is written as new files.

6
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:31.084
Copy on write finds every file that holds a refunded row, reads it whole, and writes a new copy with the change applied.

7
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:42.955
The 30 refunds touched all three files: 3.1 megabytes written, and 299,970 unchanged rows copied to change 30.

8
00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:46.704
Readers still see plain data files, so reads stay fast.

9
00:00:46.704 --> 00:00:50.113
It suits a table read far more often than it changes.

10
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:53.307
Merge on read leaves the data files alone.

11
00:00:53.307 --> 00:01:00.459
It writes the 30 new rows into one small file, and a delete file that lists the old rows by position.

12
00:01:00.633 --> 00:01:04.341
That's 6.4 kilobytes of rows and 7.4 of deletes.

13
00:01:04.341 --> 00:01:11.292
The cost moves to readers: every scan reads the delete files and skips the rows they list.

14
00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:15.130
Corrections every few minutes pile up small files.

15
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:23.555
One day in the lab ends up in 15 data files of about 44 kilobytes, plus 12 delete files that every scan must apply.

16
00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:30.403
Compaction rewrites them into one file of about 630 kilobytes, applying the deletes on the way.

17
00:01:30.403 --> 00:01:33.773
The rows stay the same; only the layout changes.

18
00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:38.974
The 15 small files stay on disk, because older snapshots still list them.

19
00:01:38.974 --> 00:01:45.628
Expiring old snapshots deletes the files only they used, and time travel to those snapshots ends.

20
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:56.175
Files never change, so every correction is paid for: by the writer with copy on write, or by every reader with merge on read, until compaction clears the debt.
